---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<Prose
  title="Contact"
  description={`Get in touch with the ${SITE.name} team — corrections, guide requests, privacy questions and press.`}
  lede="One inbox, read by a human. Corrections get priority."
>
  <p>
    The fastest way to reach us is email:
    <strong><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></strong>. We aim to
    reply within three working days.
  </p>

  <h2>What to send where</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>If you want to…</th>
        <th>Put this in the subject line</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Report something we got wrong</td>
        <td><code>Correction — [guide name]</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Request a guide for a problem you keep hitting</td>
        <td><code>Guide request</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Ask about your data, cookies or ad personalisation</td>
        <td><code>Privacy</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Report a copyright or accessibility issue</td>
        <td><code>Legal</code> or <code>Accessibility</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Talk about advertising or partnerships</td>
        <td><code>Business</code></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If a guide is wrong, tell us which step and what happened instead. We'd
    rather fix it than defend it. Confirmed corrections are applied to the
    animation and the written steps together, and the guide's "last reviewed"
    date is updated — see our <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we can't help with</h2>
  <p>
    We can't diagnose your specific repair remotely, and we can't offer
    professional plumbing, electrical, legal or medical advice. If a job feels
    beyond you, or the guide's warning section applies to your situation, please
    call a qualified professional in your area.
  </p>
</Prose>
